# The Pager executes these directly, and bash on the device fails on CRLF with
# "$'\r': command not found" / "not a valid identifier" — which is exactly how a Windows
# clone broke a device install on 2026-11-04. Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true,
# so without this file a Windows checkout gets CRLF even though the repo stores LF, and
# nothing in the repo or the harness can detect it: the gates all run on the checkout that
# was committed from, never on the one that was copied to the device.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
